{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"The pin expects exactly `1, 2, 3` followed by `int(11)`. I reproduced the defect with a guest-side loop counter: after `array_unshift`, the walker emits `1, 2,` then the prepended zeros, and then repeats `1, 2, zeros`. So this is an unbounded lowering/runtime iteration bug, not merely a slow finite case. The likely cause is that `array_unshift` rebuilds the array by dereferencing slots, while by-reference foreach advances by the old numeric key; I’m validating that by preserving slot markers and advancing from the current marker."}}
