{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"cat > collab/1793560000000-engineer-p4-foreach016.gpt-6-luna.findings.md <<'EOF'\n# foreach_016 hang: diagnosis and fix\n\n## Diagnosis\n\n\"'`Zend/tests/foreach_016.phpt` pins `1'\"\\\\n2\\\\n3\\\\nint(11)\"'`. Before the change, the PHP AST walker stalled; adding a guest-side iteration counter showed an unbounded repeated sequence (`1`, `2`, prepended zeros, then `1`, `2`, ...).\n\nThe lowering advanced by the current numeric key. `array_unshift` rebuilds the array and renumbers numeric keys, while the old prelude copy loop read slots through `php/array-get`, dereferencing and discarding reference markers. The old key can then name a newly prepended element, so by-reference foreach loses the identity of its current element and can revisit the condition that calls `array_unshift`.\n\n## Fix\n\n- `lower-foreach-ref` passes its current marker to `php/fe-next`.\n- `php/fe-next` finds that marker in the mutated array and resumes at the following ordinal. If the body removed that marker, it retains the existing key/ordinal fallback behavior.\n- `array_unshift` now copies raw slots when rebuilding the array, preserving reference markers as they move with their elements.\n\nNo shared `yin.vm/*` files or engine semantics changed. No architect action is needed.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Pinned fixture output from the walker and all four VMs: `1'\"\\\\n2\\\\n3\\\\nint(11)\"'`.\n- Warm isolated walker run: 481 ms.\n- Full quick PHPT selection: completed all 271 entries in about 46 seconds. It reports 108 pass, 48 unsupported, and 115 existing mismatches elsewhere; `foreach_016` is not among failures.\n- Consumers: `yang.php.antlr.class-model-test`, `yang.php.antlr.objects-test`, and `yang.php.antlr.generators-test`: 13 tests, 1,189 assertions, 0 failures/errors.\n- `cljstyle check` clean on both touched files; clj-kondo reports 0 errors/warnings; `git diff --check` clean.\n\nThe broader e2e namespace run was stopped while it competed with other JVM test processes. The dedicated complete PHPT quick-selection test and the consumer suites above were run to completion.\nEOF\n\ngit status --short --branch && git diff --check && git diff --stat'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
